are the ones that are not ordinary crate dependencies or that deserve a note.

scrcpy-server (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy)
  Copyright Genymobile and contributors. Apache License 2.0.
  The upstream-built scrcpy-server jar is downloaded at build time
  (phone-cam4linux/build.rs, SHA-256 pinned), embedded in the binaries, and pushed
  to the phone at run time. It is not modified. The video-socket and
  control-socket wire formats implemented in phone-cam4linux/src were derived by
  reading its source.

OpenH264 (https://github.com/cisco/openh264)
  Copyright Cisco Systems, Inc. BSD 2-Clause License.
  Compiled from source through the `openh264` crate (feature `source`) and linked
  statically. Note: Cisco's royalty coverage for H.264 applies only to the binary
  releases Cisco distributes, not to builds from source; H.264 licensing in your
  jurisdiction is your responsibility.

FFmpeg (optional, `--features ffmpeg`) (https://ffmpeg.org)
  LGPL-2.1-or-later / GPL-2.0-or-later depending on how your system copy was
  built. Linked dynamically from the system only when the feature is enabled;
  nothing from FFmpeg is distributed with this project.

ONNX Runtime (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime)
  Copyright Microsoft Corporation. MIT License.
  Used by pc4l-gui's built-in transcription model (feature `local-model`, on by
  default) through the `ort` crate (MIT/Apache-2.0), which downloads prebuilt
  ONNX Runtime binaries from pyke.io at build time (https://github.com/pykeio/ort).

Dawn (https://dawn.googlesource.com/dawn)
  Copyright The Dawn & Tint Authors. BSD 3-Clause License.
  ONNX Runtime's WebGPU execution provider; shipped as libwebgpu_dawn.so next to
  pc4l-gui in the release archives.

GLM-OCR (https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-OCR)
  Copyright Zhipu AI (Z.ai). MIT License.
  ONNX export: https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/GLM-OCR-ONNX (MIT License).
  Not included in the binaries: downloaded on first use into the user's cache
  (SHA-256 verified against the manifest in crates/pc4l-gui/src/local/mod.rs) or
  shipped as a separate release archive.

oar-ocr (https://github.com/GreatV/oar-ocr)
  Copyright Wang Xin and contributors. Apache License 2.0.
  The GLM-OCR image preprocessing ("smart resize" and patch ordering) and the
  MRoPE position-id construction in crates/pc4l-gui/src/local/glmocr.rs are
  ported from its oar-ocr-vl crate.

egui / eframe (https://github.com/emilk/egui)
  Copyright Emil Ernerfeldt. MIT License or Apache License 2.0.

v4l2loopback (https://github.com/umlaeute/v4l2loopback)
  GNU General Public License v2.0. A kernel module the user installs separately;
  this project talks to it through the V4L2 device interface only and neither
  links nor distributes it. contrib/ carries configuration snippets for it.
